# Cargo / Rust build artifacts.
#
# `/target/` covers any future root-level build output (none today —
# the wz Rust workspace lives under `crates/`). `crates/target/` is
# the wz workspace's own build output. `vendor/sce/target/` is the
# vendored SCE submodule's build output (submodule itself is tracked
# as a gitlink; only its target/ stays local).
/target/

# Headless round runner (scripts/round-runner.sh): verdict file, logs, lock.
# NOT under .git/ -- the agent that writes the verdict is blocked from that
# path by the permission layer, which a headless round cannot answer.
/.round/
crates/target/
# R311y666 — and WITHOUT the trailing slash, because a build cache may be a
# SYMLINK rather than a directory and `crates/target/` does not match one. This
# tree's is (`crates/target -> ~/.buildcache/...`), and it reached the index of
# a `git add -A crates` before this line existed: build output, and a
# machine-local absolute path, in a committed file.
crates/target
vendor/sce/target/
# R311be — deploy/mcu-qemu-demo is a standalone workspace
# (cross-compile to thumbv7m-none-eabi); its target/ is build
# output identical in policy to crates/target/.
deploy/mcu-qemu-demo/target/
# R311hl — deploy/mcu-noheap-probe is a third standalone workspace
# (no-heap registry runtime proof; Layer Q.0). Same target/ policy.
deploy/mcu-noheap-probe/target/
# Stage 5 — deploy/mcu-session-acceptor is the fourth standalone
# workspace (acceptor session e2e bin; Layer Q.4). Same target/ policy.
deploy/mcu-session-acceptor/target/
# R311mi — deploy/mcu-multicast-e2e is the fifth standalone workspace
# (multicast footprint bin; Layer Q.5). Same target/ policy.
deploy/mcu-multicast-e2e/target/
# R311y269 — Layer Q.6 (the loopback-multicast QEMU runtime proof) builds the
# SAME bin with a different feature set, and cargo uplifts every feature variant
# to the same final path — so Q.6's ELF used to overwrite Q.5's footprint
# artifact. Q.6 now gets its own CARGO_TARGET_DIR; same target/ policy.
deploy/mcu-multicast-e2e/target-loopback/
# R311y27 — deploy/mcu-freertos-demo is the standalone FreeRTOS-profile
# workspace (boot e2e; Layer Q.frt). Same target/ policy.
deploy/mcu-freertos-demo/target/
# R311y31 — deploy/zephyr-app/rust is the standalone Zephyr-profile Rust
# staticlib (Path-B boot e2e; Layer Qz). Its target/ is the cargo cross
# output (the west build dir lives outside the repo). Same target/ policy.
deploy/zephyr-app/rust/target/
# R311y22 — xtask is the sixth standalone workspace (the codegen SSOT
# that regenerates out/**; pulls sce-build/libxml2, kept out of the main
# build). Same target/ policy. Its Cargo.lock IS committed (reproducible
# regen), same as the deploy bins.
xtask/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock policy: COMMITTED for the wz Rust workspace
# (`crates/Cargo.lock`) per Cargo's recommendation for binary-
# producing workspaces and for reproducible Layer 3 wire-interop
# tests across CI / dev / production. SCE submodule's lock file is
# managed by SCE. The root-level `/Cargo.lock` ignore is defensive —
# no workspace lives at the repo root today, but the rule prevents
# accidental commit if one is added later without a paired
# workspace-policy review.
/Cargo.lock

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Mnemosyne — atomic store sidecar is workspace state; commit it (the
# audit trail lives there). GENERATED.md is derived but typically also
# committed so reviewers can read it without running the CLI.
# .atomic/  ← do NOT ignore; it IS the source of truth post Round 251.
#
# watching-zenoh hybrid carry: the 13 prose docs in mnemosyne.toml ARE
# the human-readable surface — GENERATED.md is NOT used here. Atomic
# store stays as audit-only ledger; the cascade-generated GENERATED.md
# is a byproduct of every MCP mutate primitive (MCP has no
# --no-regenerate; only mnemosyne-cli does). We don't track it.
docs/GENERATED.md

# Local Claude Code state — settings.local.json, scheduled_tasks.lock,
# transcripts, etc. Team-shared .claude/settings.json (if introduced)
# would carve out via an explicit `!.claude/settings.json` exception.
.claude/

# Activity logs (local working notes; outside mnemosyne workspace).
# Cross-session handoff lives in the atomic changelog (audit-traced);
# notes/ is a local working cache only.
notes/

# Claude-facing analysis / scratch docs (audits, codegen-surface notes).
# Local working artifacts, not part of the tracked design surface (the
# atomic store is the SSOT). Previously-tracked files are untracked via
# `git rm --cached`; they stay on disk as local references.
claudedocs/

# Python bytecode from the scripts/lib gate modules
__pycache__/

# cargo-sweep's build-mode timestamp (scripts/gc-build-artifacts.sh). Written
# next to the workspace manifest before a wrapped build and consumed by the
# sweep after it; purely local scratch, never a committed artifact.
crates/sweep.timestamp
